<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec green coffee imports up 47.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec green coffee imports up 47.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in December totalled 23,959 tonnes, up 47.2 percent from the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 193 tonnes in December against 164 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of green coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Dec 96	   Nov 96	   Dec 95</p>
<p> Total	   23,959	   26,411	   16,282</p>
<p> Indonesia	4,506	    5,949	    3,337</p>
<p> Colombia	 5,380	    4,462	    4,530</p>
<p> Brazil	   7,837	    8,618	    3,251</p>
<p> Guatemala	  836		844		398</p>
<p> Honduras	   378		155		223</p>
<p>Cumulative green coffee imports in 1996 were 326,388 tonnes, up 9.0 percent from 299,555 tonnes in the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Dec 96	  Nov 96	   Dec 95</p>
<p> Total		193	     386		164</p>
<p>Cumulative roasted coffee imports in 1996 were 3,270 tonnes, up 57.6 percent from 2,075 tonnes the year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 6179</p>
</text>
